    "gap_reduction_ratio_val": 0.7331,
    "clinical_diagnosis_explanation": "In all-hours evaluation, unconstrained Random Forest appears to substantially lead constrained HGB (Val PR-AUC gap = 0.0903, Test gap = 0.1040). However, 31.6% of all hours occur inside active episodes, post-episode 18h recovery, or 72h refractory periods. During recovery hours, patient vitals and symptoms remain elevated, but the simulator assigns zero hazard for a new onset. Unconstrained trees exploit non-monotonic splits on arbitrary feature combinations to artificially suppress risk predictions during recovery, whereas constrained HGB is bound by pathophysiological domain priors to maintain elevated risk when vitals/symptoms are high, receiving false-positive penalties. When evaluated strictly on true 'at-risk' clinical decision hours, the RF vs HGB gap collapses from 0.0903 down to 0.0241 on validation (and from 0.1040 to 0.0305 on holdout test), demonstrating that constrained HGB performs nearly on par with unconstrained RF during actual at-risk periods."
  },
